# [SEAT](../wg/seat.html)

## Summary

The SEAT working group met at IETF 127 to review progress on working group deliverables and candidate solution drafts, discuss security models and privacy considerations, and gauge working group consensus on adopting core protocol and architecture documents. 

Key updates were presented on the adopted use cases draft (`draft-ietf-seat-use-cases`), the architecture draft (`draft-many-seat-architecture`), early attestation (`draft-fossati-seat-early-attestation-09`), and forward TLS binding (`draft-fossati-seat-expat-05`). Following discussion on working group progress and technical trade-offs, the chairs conducted indicative adoption polls for `draft-fossati-seat-expat-05`, `draft-fossati-seat-early-attestation-09`, and `draft-many-seat-architecture`, all showing strong support to proceed to formal list calls.

