### Binding Attestation to Forward TLS Connections
- **Presentation:** [Binding Attestation to Forward TLS Connections](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-seat-binding-attestation-to-forward-tls-connections-03)
- **Presenter:** Akira Tsukamoto
- **Draft:** `draft-fossati-seat-expat-05`

- **Presentation Summary:**
  - Akira Tsukamoto presented the "EXPAT" approach, which separates the attestation handshake from subsequent application data paths.
  - A relying party connects to a dedicated attestation endpoint inside the target environment over an attested TLS session to establish derived forward identity key pairs using TLS 1.3 key exporters and exported authenticators.
  - Standard, unmodified application servers (e.g., AI inference workloads) can then reuse standard TLS connections with the provisioned certificates without requiring code modifications to support attestation protocols directly.

- **Discussion:**
  - Muhammad Usama Sardar inquired about aligning exported authenticator mechanisms between related drafts to ensure complementary designs.

